              },
              {
                "id": "studio-the-scroll-27",
                "type": "heading",
                "values": {
                  "anchor": "",
                  "displayCondition": null,
                  "selectable": true,
                  "draggable": true,
                  "duplicatable": true,
                  "deletable": true,
                  "hideable": true,
                  "_meta": {
                    "htmlID": "u_content_heading_1",
                    "htmlClassNames": "u_content_heading"
                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "I use AI every day, but not the way you’d expect",
                  "fontSize": "18px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Helvetica",
                    "value": "helvetica,sans-serif"
                  },
                  "color": "#1A1A1A",
                  "textAlign": "left",
                  "lineHeight": "110%",
                  "containerPadding": "4px 32px 8px",
                  "headingType": "h2"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "studio-the-scroll-28",
                "type": "text",
                "values": {
                  "anchor": "",
                  "displayCondition": null,
                  "selectable": true,
                  "draggable": true,
                  "duplicatable": true,
                  "deletable": true,
                  "hideable": true,
                  "_meta": {
                    "htmlID": "u_content_text_11",
                    "htmlClassNames": "u_content_text"
                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "Most people’s AI workflow looks like this: open a chatbot, ask it to write something, get something generic back, rewrite it all, and wonder what the point was. That was me a year ago.<br><br>What changed was working out where each tool fits in my process:<br><br>•&nbsp; <strong>Better inputs beat better prompts.</strong> What you feed the tool matters more than how you ask.<br>•&nbsp; <strong>It’s a thinking partner, not a ghostwriter.</strong> I use it to find holes in my ideas.<br>•&nbsp; <strong>Your voice is the thing it can’t copy.</strong> I write drafts myself and use AI to edit.<br>•&nbsp; <strong>Automate the busywork, not the creative part.</strong><br><br><strong>Bottom line:</strong> AI won’t fix weak content, but it will speed you up once you know what you’re making.",
                  "fontSize": "13px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Helvetica",
                    "value": "helvetica,sans-serif"
                  },
                  "color": "#1A1A1A",
                  "textAlign": "left",
                  "lineHeight": "160%",
                  "containerPadding": "4px 32px 8px"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "studio-the-scroll-29",
                "type": "button",
                "values": {
                  "anchor": "",
                  "displayCondition": null,
                  "selectable": true,
                  "draggable": true,
                  "duplicatable": true,
                  "deletable": true,
                  "hideable": true,
                  "_meta": {
                    "htmlID": "u_content_button_1",
